I was never talking about the players vision, but the vision of the
computer. YOU started the talk about the players vision.


To quote the source code in do_light_sources()

	/*
	 * Check for moved light sources.  It may be possible to
	 * save some effort if an object has not moved, but not in
	 * the current setup -- we need to recalculate for every
	 * vision recalc.
	 */

what does this tell us?
if we don't call do_light sources, they are not updated. As it is not
called in vision.c
vision_recalc(control)
{
... else if (Blind) {
goto skip
}
we don't have the light sources updated and therefore the position is
not changed and the player can step outside of the lighted area.


